Rendered by the kernel itself, not by godel.py, and that is the whole point:
`godel.py --verify` diffs its parser against the writer rather than against
its own expectations. Captured from one driven QEMU session --

  drive.py "godel verdict /tmp/vg" "godel ledger 3" "godel clade"

-- after a real signed verdict was filed. Re-capture the same way when the
kernel's rendering changes; a fixture set edited by hand is a fixture set
that agrees with whoever edited it.
